---
layout: page
---
{%- comment -%}
Content pages (about, blog posts, CV entries, USPs, fun facts, projects): the text in a
centred column with an "On this page" list beside it that follows the reader, the same
layout as on becker-consulting.se. The styles (.article-layout, .article, .toc, .prose)
and the script that marks the current section come from there, see site.sharedAssets.
The list shows when a page has two or more <h2>s; they get ids here.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign body = content | headingIds -%}
{%- assign toc = body | toc -%}
<div class="article-layout">
    <article class="article{% if article_class %} {{ article_class }}{% endif %}" data-section="{{ title }}" data-source="{{ page.url | absolute_url }}">
        {{ body }}
    </article>
    {%- if toc.size > 1 %}
    <aside class="toc no-print" aria-label="{{ headings.ui.on_this_page }}">
        <p class="label">{{ headings.ui.on_this_page }}</p>
        {% for item in toc %}<a href="#{{ item.id }}">{{ item.text }}</a>
        {% endfor %}
    </aside>
    {%- endif %}
</div>
